  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_010: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, weighted → 0.573 acc), evidence is very sparse. The most informative next step is to isolate a single design variable from the current best. Config_007 is identical to config_010 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, giving a clean A/B test of the fusion strategy while holding all other factors (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer aggregation) constant. This clarifies whether weighted or concat fusion is the better mechanism for combining modality representations—a choice that will affect every subsequent multimodal experiment. If concat outperforms weighted, it opens a new promising direction; if weighted is confirmed, we can confidently fix that parameter and explore other axes (image encoder, RNA encoder, aggregation) in remaining experiments. Expected cost is comparable to config_010 (~6.5–7 GPU hours) since the architecture is identical, making this a low-risk, high-information experiment early in the budget."
